@scene chapter_5b_card_catalogue

background: ancient_library.png
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"You have one foot toward the west door when the Cataloguer's voice stops you, gentle and certain."

background: cataloguer

npc Cataloguer:
"A moment, child. You can OPEN my book now. You cannot yet KEEP one."
"Sit with a blind woman a while. Let me show you how knowledge is filed when you cannot see the shelves."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE CARD CATALOGUE"
"dict access · .get · in · keys/values · tuples · sets"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — ASK BY NAME —"
"She turns the grimoire toward you. Names glow along the margins, each roped to an incantation."

npc Cataloguer:
"A dictionary is pairs. A name, and what the name points to. Say the name in square brackets; receive the value."
"And when you fear the book may not know a name, ask with GET, and hand it a word for its ignorance. Then a gap is a shrug, not a scream."

interactive: catalogue_lookup_get

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — WHAT THE BOOK HOLDS —"

npc Cataloguer:
"Sometimes you needn't fetch a thing at all. You need only ask: is it HERE?"
"The word 'in' asks the book of its names. And 'len' tells you how many pairs it keeps."

interactive: catalogue_membership

npc Cataloguer:
"Now file one yourself. A name, and the incantation it should summon. Bind them."

interactive: catalogue_forge

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — THE SEALED SCROLL —"
"She lifts a slim scroll bound in wax, and will not let you break the seal."

npc Cataloguer:
"Not everything should be changeable. Some records must be FIXED, or they are worthless."
"This is a tuple. Read it like a list — but try to change it, and it refuses. A sealed scroll. Once written, forever."

interactive: catalogue_tuples

npc Cataloguer:
"Learn which of your tools bend, and which are sealed. Confuse them and you will corrupt a record you meant to keep safe."

interactive: catalogue_sort_mutable

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — THE UNREPEATING ROSTER —"
"She spreads a guild roster on the desk. Where two names match, one quietly fades."

npc Cataloguer:
"And last — the roster that keeps no one twice. A set."
"Drop a hundred names in; only the distinct remain. You met this at the Dragon's Trial, though you did not know its name: no two souls the same."

interactive: catalogue_sets

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — DOES THE BOOK KNOW IT? —"
"She slides a closed grimoire toward you and names a spell."

npc Cataloguer:
"Before you fetch, you ask. Tell me true — does the book hold this name, or not?"

system system:
"MISSION"
"Return True if the grimoire holds a spell under `name`, else False."

mission: catalogue_lookup

npc Cataloguer:
"Just so. Now the question that has been troubling me."

dialogue:
"— COMBINE IT — HOW MANY, TRULY? —"
"She taps the swollen spine of the great book."

npc Cataloguer:
"My book has grown fat, and I suspect half its names point to the SAME incantation."
"Pull every incantation, drop the repeats, and count what truly remains. Dict, and set, in one breath."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Return how many distinct incantations (values) the grimoire holds."

mission: catalogue_distinct

dialogue:
"You gather the values, let the set swallow the duplicates, and speak the count."
"The Cataloguer exhales, as if a long-held worry has finally been filed away."

npc Cataloguer:
"Fewer than I feared, and now I KNOW. You've the makings of an archivist, child."

background: cataloguer

npc Cataloguer:
"Before you go — one card, drawn cold. The whole catalogue at once."

interactive: catalogue_final_recall

npc Cataloguer:
"Values out, duplicates gone, counted. That is the catalogue entire, and you carry it now."
"Go west now, truly. The loom-woman is waiting, and she'll not make it easy — she never speaks plainly."
"Listen past her riddles. The lesson underneath is always kind."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Card Catalogue"
"Mastered: dict access · .get · in · len · tuples (sealed) · sets (distinct)"

reward:
xp: 75
gold: 45
achievement: NO TWO THE SAME

next:
chapter_6_riddle_weaver
